  "notes": [
   "Award matched to the 42-unit Certificate of Achievement in Graphic and Interactive Design: Foothill is on quarters, and 42 quarter units falls within 24Q to fewer than 45Q. The other certificates on the page (12-16 units) are below this range.",
   "The certificate section states it is awarded upon completion of the core and support courses (the 42-unit major list), so blocks are read from the Core and Support Courses list; general education is not required.",
   "Support courses carry no units beside them in the text; units recorded as null. The support list is printed under topical subheadings (Animation, Art, Game Design, Graphic Design, Screen Printing, Web Development, Visual Storytelling, Independent Study), all under one 'Select 16 units from the following' rule, so recorded as one choose_units block.",
   "Catalog codes like GID 1A, GID 44A, ART 4A are treated as the same courses as closed-list GID 001A, GID 044A, ART 004A (zero-padded format).",
   "PHOT 5H (honors twin) and GID 70R-73R (independent study) are not in the closed list; marked catalog additions.",
   "Program Learning Outcomes are printed once for the program as a whole; the certificate shares them.",
   "The associate degree's 90-unit minimum belongs to the AA, not this certificate; degree_total left null."
